Keep `late clarification`, `failed fallback timing`, and unresolved join failure independently visible when coordination reroute or fallback behavior is under review.
Keep `scenario_id`, `run_id`, `cohort_id`, `trace_id`, and `artifact_version` stable across coordination artifacts that remain linked.
If multiple coordination artifacts must be merged, keep one explicit join rule for precedence, compatibility, freshness, completeness, unresolved join failure, and downgrade behavior.
Reject incompatible merges that would weaken a stronger coordination artifact, and preserve upstream source IDs and `artifact_version` in the surviving join result.

